The checkin app will allow a coach to cancelan individual lesson, or any lessons ~~that day~~ *from today to the end of this week (the Week tab, see C_Rinkside Cancel Several Lessons.md)*. When canceling the coach will be asked if they want to release or hold the slots. 
    Hold: ~~means they are coach held~~ the time stays closed (a held lesson time) *(revised 2026-10-13, ADR-031)*
    Release: means they are rebookable by othr students
    *2026-11-08 (owner; ADR-009):* cancelling the whole week doesn't ask. Every booked lesson and open time left in the
    week is held closed.
*Design:* cancelling one lesson is under the "..." button on its card, kept away from Present and No-show. It always
confirms, names the family who will be emailed, and asks Release for rebooking or Hold it closed (ADR-009 d5a).
A lesson that has started can't be cancelled, and cancelling needs signal.
*Rinkside cancelling rules:*
  Added 2026-09-22. The rinkside app is used at the rink on a phone. It offers cancellation in two places:
    1. A cancel section — the whole day, part of a day, the whole week, part of a week, or specific lessons
       (see C_Rinkside Cancel Several Lessons.md; "part of a day/week" is a multi-select of lessons, see cancelation.md).
    2. The check-in list — each lesson has a cancel action under its "…" button, kept away from Present and No-show,
       so a single lesson can be cancelled from either place. *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.*
  It is the same cancellation as on the website: the same release-or-hold question, it skips lessons that already
    happened, anything larger than one lesson gets the same preview-then-accept step, and families are told once.
  The rinkside app cannot cancel without a connection. *Decided by the owner, 2026-09-30.* With no signal, every cancel
    action — in the check-in list and the cancel section — is disabled, with the note "Cancelling needs a connection."
    The Week tab shows no lessons offline, only that the week needs a connection (owner, 2026-11-09, R5).
    Check-ins are queued offline because they record something that already happened; a cancellation changes something
    that is about to happen, and a queued one would not reach the family until the phone reconnected — possibly after
    they had left for the rink. It also needs the server for the preview.
  A cancel from the check-in list always asks for confirmation, even for one lesson. *Decided by the owner, 2026-09-30.*
    Cancel sits under the lesson's "…" button, away from Present and No-show (the design; *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.*), and choosing it
    opens a confirmation rather than cancelling. This goes further than the website, which only requires
    confirmation above a single lesson. The reason: on a phone held rinkside, often with gloves on, a mis-tap is
    likely, and a cancel cannot be undone — release cancels the family's place and a hold is permanent.
    For the confirmation to actually stop a mis-tap, it has to be something a second mis-tap cannot complete:
      It names the lesson — student, date and time — so the coach sees what they are about to cancel.
      Its confirming action is not where the original tap landed, so a repeated tap in the same spot cannot cancel.
      Dismissing it keeps the lesson. The safe choice is the easy one.
      Release-or-hold is chosen inside the same dialog, so a single-lesson cancel is still one confirmation, not two
        prompts.
  Settled questions (ADR-009 Open): ~~Can the rinkside app cancel with no signal?~~ Settled 2026-09-30: no.
    ~~A mis-tap guard on the check-in list.~~ Settled 2026-09-30: yes — every cancel from the
    check-in list confirms, even for one lesson.
  *(from ADR-009 decision 5a and Open, moved 2026-11-08)*

*Design (today.html), the Today tab:*
  A progress bar: how many of today's lessons are recorded, and who's next.
  Each lesson card: time, skater, length. Present and No-show buttons once the lesson is within 10 minutes of starting;
  before that it shows "Starts at <time>". A recorded lesson shows Present or No-show with the time. There is no Undo on the phone: a mistake is corrected on
    the website's Lessons page (see Coach lesson list, "Why corrections are on the website"). *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.*
  A held slot shows "Held slot", closed to everyone.
  Tabs along the bottom: Today, Week, Account (see C_Rinkside Account.md).
  No signal: see C_Rinkside Offline.md.

Present and No-show:
  The app offers two outcomes per lesson, present or absent, rather than check-in alone (owner, 2026-08-30;
  ADR-014 d6). A recorded no-show is what lets ~~the end-of-day report~~ *Payments, the lesson list and the unpaid reminder (the end-of-day report is Phase 2, owner 2026-11-11)* tell "didn't come" apart from "not recorded yet".
  When this was decided, what a no-show costs was still open: the payment reminder followed a check-in only, so a
  student who reserved ice and didn't appear was billed nothing while one who attended was billed. That is very likely
  backwards from a coach's point of view, since the ice was held either way, but it is a business decision, and until it
  was made the app would show the coach a button whose consequence was nothing.
  *Settled the same day by ADR-015 decision 5: a no-show is charged under the same rule as a late cancellation.*
  A coach can record a no-show that costs nothing until Phase 2: ADR-015 decided the charge but scheduled it for
  Phase 2. The button records a real outcome and feeds ~~the end-of-day report~~ *Payments and the lesson list* from day one, and starts carrying money
  later.
  *(from ADR-014 §6 and Consequences, moved 2026-11-08)*

The app needs to also have a sign in screen where the coach is validated that they are who they say they are. 
*Design (signin.html):* the same login email and password as the website (ADR-023 d2, d7: only a coach's account gets in). It's BladeBook's own sign-in form, sending straight to Cognito (ADR-023 d11, 2026-11-09). The page says the app shows today's lessons, records attendance and cancels lessons; the schedule, students and payments stay on the website.
*"Your dashboard" link (owner, 2026-10-21; ADR-023 d8):* at the top of every screen after sign-in, back to the coach website's
Today page in the same tab; it asks for the password if the rinkside sign-in is over 60 minutes old.
  Every rinkside screen after sign-in has a "Your dashboard" link at the top. It opens the coach website's Today page
  (/coach) in the same tab. The sign-in screen doesn't show it. If the rinkside sign-in is more than 60 minutes old,
  the website asks for the password first.
  *(from ADR-023 §8, decided by the owner 2026-10-21; moved 2026-11-08)*


